From cab99f060f6e7add21e427e663410a8e6738afbe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 03:22:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] services: whoever turns Samba on is told the address, the
 user and the password

Samba is off by default and, when it is turned on, has a user (libreelec) and a
generated password. Both were shown in LibreELEC Settings > Services > Samba, but
nothing said so: a person who turned it on in the first-run wizard or in the
settings got a switch that went on and no way in, and had to find the password
by looking at the page afterwards. (Reported by a user who could not copy an
update file to the system.)

Turning it on, in the wizard or in the settings, now shows a dialog with the
address to open on Windows, Mac or Linux, the user and the password, says where
to read them again, and that the same login copies an update file into the
Update share. Where the generated login is not known yet it says where to look.
Turning other settings of Samba does not show it again.
